{
  "$comment": "Stored-record versions and recovery decisions (spec 030, REQ-DB-011, REQ-DB-012, ADR-0049). `decisions`: the one Rust decision `stored_record(schema, current)` mapping a version to `use`, `upgrade` or `discard` (crates/rust-core/tests/stored_record_fixtures.rs, crates/tran-uniffi/tests/stored_record_fixtures.rs, the native and TypeScript parity tests). `records`: what a device really has stored, driven through each platform's real store (iOS StoredRecordTests.swift, Android StoredRecordTest.kt; TypeScript: packages/core-ts/tests). `raw` is the stored JSON; `expected` is what the store hands back (null: treated as absent); `kept` is whether the stored record is still there after the read: a record is never rewritten on read, a newer version is left for the app that wrote it, and only an unreadable record (bad bytes or field types, or a `schema` that is not a whole number from 1 to 4294967295) is deleted. A record without `schema` is the unversioned first release (version 1). Push has no JSON on either device: each key is one preference (iOS UserDefaults TranPushSchema / TranPushRegisteredToken / TranPushRegisteredAt; Android tran.push schema / registered_token / registered_at_unix_s), written with the JSON value's type.",
  "currentSchemas": {
    "session": 2,
    "push": 2,
    "config": 2
  },
  "decisions": [
    {
      "name": "matching version 1 uses record directly",
      "schema": 1,
      "current": 1,
      "action": "use"
    },
    {
      "name": "matching version 2 uses record directly",
      "schema": 2,
      "current": 2,
      "action": "use"
    },
    {
      "name": "older version 1 with current 2 upgrades record",
      "schema": 1,
      "current": 2,
      "action": "upgrade"
    },
    {
      "name": "older version 2 with current 3 upgrades record",
      "schema": 2,
      "current": 3,
      "action": "upgrade"
    },
    {
      "name": "newer version 3 with current 2 discards record",
      "schema": 3,
      "current": 2,
